                    from the 60Hz default, you're using a cable that can't carry the
                    full bandwidth, browser hardware acceleration is off, or your
                    laptop is in a power-saving mode.
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-q">How accurate is a browser-based refresh rate test?</div>
                <div class="faq-a">
                    requestAnimationFrame is tied to your display's vsync, so under
                    normal conditions readings are accurate to within ±1–2Hz.
                    Background tabs, high CPU load, or OS-level frame pacing can
                    cause temporary dips — which is exactly what the stability grade
                    and frame-time chart are designed to surface.
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-q">What does the Stability Grade actually measure?</div>
                <div class="faq-a">
